# Your own Suricata rules. Run ./update-rules.sh after editing this file.
# Use sid numbers from 1000000 up so they don't clash with the downloaded rules.
# Rule syntax: https://docs.suricata.io/en/latest/rules/intro.html
#
# Example (remove the # to turn it on): alert on every ping.
# alert icmp any any -> any any (msg:"ARGUS ping seen"; itype:8; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
#
# Example: alert on a web request for /etc/passwd.
# alert http any any -> any any (msg:"ARGUS request for /etc/passwd"; http.uri; content:"/etc/passwd"; sid:1000002; rev:1;)
